title: mf uuid
tags: [[CLI command]] [[File tracking]]
kind: reference
summary: Print the UUID of the metarecord standing for each path (the inverse of `mf path`); exit 1 if one has none

The metarecord at a path, found and never created: `mf path` answers the other way. A
path is taken as `mf watch check` takes it — an existing one is canonicalised and made
relative to the repository's root, one gone from disk is read as repo-root-relative
when it starts with `/` (an orphan's stale `mfr_path`). To create a path's metarecord:
`mf metarecord add --path` ([[Recording a path]]).
